to the workshop.

00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:01.371
Shou Sugi Ban.

00:23:01.371 --> 00:23:04.860
It is a Japanese wood preserving technique.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:11.830
It's already been mentioned a couple of times
in the YouTube comments, and I'm very curious about this.

00:23:11.830 --> 00:23:21.087
It's about burning the surface of the wood,
which makes it harder to penetrate for fungus, and bugs.

00:23:21.087 --> 00:23:22.561
So, it's more weatherproof.

00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:38.540
Yeah, after after the burning, we will oil it.

00:23:43.480 --> 00:23:45.680
I think we're gonna try linseed oil.

00:24:05.791 --> 00:24:07.947
